[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: RO3 System Requirements (REQ)
UID: DOC-RO3-REQ
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: About

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Project: RO3 (Ragnarok 3 in ROOGuildApp). Strictly isolated from ROO (Ragnarok Origin): every relation in this document points at RO3 nodes only. Origin counterparts appear as plain text (counterpart …) and are never links.
Source: SSOT requirements/req (published only). Each REQ Parent-links to its RO3 USR via linked_from.
Published nodes: 22 (REQ-RO3-001 .. REQ-RO3-022).
SSOT sync 2026-10-10 (JST): graph 91; source xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8. Published in SSOT ≠ proven; no EVD; every TST is execution_status blocked_on_tooling, evidence_status none.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Games/Access (REQ-RO3-001 .. REQ-RO3-003, REQ-RO3-018, REQ-RO3-022)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RO3-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-RO3-001: Ragnarok 3 is a known game with no setup step
STATEMENT: >>>
Ragnarok 3 is a known game with no setup step
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Games/Access
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: Game id ragnarok-3; home path /games/ragnarok-3.
acceptance_criteria: The games catalog lists Ragnarok 3 next to Origin and Adventurer Guild. | When Ragnarok 3 is enabled it counts as set up with no Discord channel mapping required. | Pages under /games/ragnarok-3 are treated as Ragnarok 3, not Origin.
source_draft: f38e137/mints-RO3.json
ssot_status: published
sot: xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8
counterpart (text only, not a link): REQ-ROO-039, REQ-ROO-042, REQ-ROO-043
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-RO3-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RO3-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-RO3-002: Ragnarok 3 pages need the game enabled and an active subscription
STATEMENT: >>>
Ragnarok 3 pages need the game enabled and an active subscription
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Games/Access
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: Applies to every Ragnarok 3 API.
acceptance_criteria: A signed-in workspace with an active subscription but without Ragnarok 3 enabled gets 403 with code game_required and gameId ragnarok-3 from any Ragnarok 3 API. | With Ragnarok 3 enabled, the Ragnarok 3 health check answers success with gameId ragnarok-3.
source_draft: f38e137/mints-RO3.json
ssot_status: published
sot: xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8
counterpart (text only, not a link): REQ-ROO-045
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-RO3-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RO3-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-RO3-003: Ragnarok 3 and Origin are kept apart in both directions, both their data and the
STATEMENT: >>>
Ragnarok 3 and Origin are kept apart in both directions, both their data and their running activity
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Games/Access
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: (none)
acceptance_criteria: A record saved through Ragnarok 3 never appears in, and never changes, Origin data for the same workspace. | A record saved through Origin never appears in, and never changes, Ragnarok 3 data for the same workspace. | No Ragnarok 3 page, request or card press reads or writes Origin data, and no Origin page, request or card press reads or writes Ragnarok 3 data. | The same Discord member can have a Ragnarok 3 roster entry and an Origin roster entry at once. | Starting, running or ending a live raid in one game never stops, pauses or changes a live raid that is already running in the other game in the same workspace, in either direction.
source_draft: f38e137/mints-RO3.json
ssot_status: published
sot: xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8
counterpart (text only, not a link): REQ-ROO-158
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-RO3-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RO3-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-RO3-018: Ragnarok 3 posts its own cards to Discord
STATEMENT: >>>
Ragnarok 3 posts its own cards to Discord
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Games/Access
priority: unspecified
type: software
constraints: Card set offered at f38e137: GvG readiness/attendance, party, party-screenshot, onboarding. The customer has not listed which cards Ragnarok 3 offers (open question Q8).
acceptance_criteria: An officer deploying a Ragnarok 3 card gets the card posted, or the existing Ragnarok 3 card updated, in the workspace's mapped Discord channel. | A Ragnarok 3 card shows only Ragnarok 3 data (roster, events, published grids, settings) and never Origin data. | Posting or updating a Ragnarok 3 card does not edit, replace or remove an Origin card. | When the channel is not mapped, the bot is unavailable or the caller is not an officer, the deploy is refused with an error and nothing is posted.
source_draft: f38e137/mints-RO3.json
ssot_status: published
sot: xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8
counterpart (text only, not a link): USR-ROO-019 (Origin deploys cards)
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-RO3-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RO3-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: REQ-RO3-022: Ragnarok 3 has no auction or request features
STATEMENT: >>>
Ragnarok 3 has no auction or request features
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
domain: Games/Access
priority: unspecified
type: business
constraints: (none)
acceptance_criteria: No Ragnarok 3 page or navigation item offers an auction, request lobby, item queue, request history, past auctions, Mimic Book or auction rewards. | Using any Ragnarok 3 page makes no call to Origin's /api/requests/* addresses. | Ragnarok 3 exposes no auction or request address of its own under /api/ragnarok-3. | No Ragnarok 3 Discord card offers an auction or request action.
source_draft: f38e137/answers-2026-10-08/mints.json
ssot_status: published
sot: xWhiteSpace/ROOGuildApp@f38e1378c7cca457fbf8de8e8355d59994f77fc8
counterpart (text only, not a link): USR-ROO-021, USR-ROO-022 (Origin auction)
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: USR-RO3-001

